{
  "analysis": "Doom boots and loads the WAD but Z_Malloc fails because the zone memory is only 600000 bytes instead of the expected ~16MB. The custom stdlib has a 1GB static heap in BSS, and basic_malloc should be able to handle large allocations. I need to find the DEFAULT_RAM value and trace what's happening during malloc to understand why the zone is so small.",
  "plan": "Search for DEFAULT_RAM and MIN_RAM definitions, inspect z_zone.c for how the zone size is reported, and add tracing to the VM for basic_malloc calls to see what size is requested and what pointer is returned. This will reveal why the zone is only 600KB.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -rn \"DEFAULT_RAM\\|MIN_RAM\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/ | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"Z_Init\\|zone memory\\|allocated for zone\\|zone_t\\|sizeof\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/z_zone.c | head -30\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,80p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/z_zone.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
